ype of the end-to-end  solution ready so that we could make the  most of this trial period so around one  month so it wasn't a lot of time and we  couldn't do um  you know very sophisticated things in  that short time so we had to be creative  a little bit and that was also an  interesting part of that project that uh  it forced us to be creative and find  solutions that  have to be good enough of course for the  trial but um not not the full thing  um  so i will focus on the data vis just for  time constraints on of the problem so  i'll go through all the requirements we  have to meet in this in this trial and  how we solved uh those requirements and  um yeah so  the first requirement was of course the  model needed to be interpretable that  was very important because our  stakeholders the traders in the  commodity team needed to really  understand why the model was making a  certain prediction so that they could  use that prediction trusted prediction  and then use it in their decision  um so the the solution we adopted for  that was simply to open the black box of  the uh machine learning model with the  database library we use plotline in this  case um so we generated a number of  graphs um i guess the the most important  one was this this is a waterfall plot  showing how the prediction of the model  the blue bar breaks down into um  contribution for each feature  so that uh our stakeholders were able to  tell that um you know this this  prediction is is mostly driven by for  example uh weather data in this region  of the planet  uh or maybe supply and demand data in  this country and so on and also see the  sign of this feature so is this variable  pushing the price up or down and so on  and then we also added more complex  graphs for example this one on the  bottom  showing again the same feature  contribution breakdown but against time  over the last 10 months  again people could see trends there are  some variables some features that change  signs change the